{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837998",
      "title": "Mixing Custom & Built-in Validation Logic",
      "sourceHash": "6452adeee4d380f44747b357ad025cd8eae271e819cf7ba51ee149432215585a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 2.16,
          "en": "So using the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 5.85,
          "en": "and the built-in validation attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.85,
          "end": 8.58,
          "en": "can be a great way of adding validation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.58,
          "end": 11.01,
          "en": "and indeed would be my recommendation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.01,
          "end": 14.4,
          "en": "for many use cases also, because it doesn't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.4,
          "end": 19.4,
          "en": "require any extra React or JavaScript logic from your side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 24.03,
          "en": "But you can of course still add such logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.03,
          "end": 26.64,
          "en": "if you want to run some extra checks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.64,
          "end": 29.16,
          "en": "beyond the default checks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.16,
          "end": 31.71,
          "en": "For example, here in the signup form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.71,
          "end": 35.15,
          "en": "I might wanna make sure that the value entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.15,
          "end": 39.33,
          "en": "in this confirm-password field matches the value entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 40.803,
          "en": "into this input field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.76,
          "end": 45.54,
          "en": "And there is no built-in attribute like matches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.54,
          "end": 49.14,
          "en": "or anything like that that would easily allow us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.14,
          "end": 51.63,
          "en": "to add this kind of check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.63,
          "end": 54.51,
          "en": "But of course, just because we're using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.51,
          "end": 57.09,
          "en": "these built-in attributes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.09,
          "end": 60.57,
          "en": "does not mean that we can't add our own logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.57,
          "end": 64.47,
          "en": "and combine that with that built-in logic here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.47,
          "end": 69.12,
          "en": "For example, here, we could add some extra state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.12,
          "end": 72.84,
          "en": "to this component to output an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.84,
          "end": 77.65,
          "en": "if the passwords are not equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.99,
          "end": 81.69,
          "en": "and have a setPasswordsAreNotEqual",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.53,
          "end": 84.24,
          "en": "state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.24,
          "end": 86.223,
          "en": "And initially this could be false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.93,
          "end": 89.49,
          "en": "And then here, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.49,
          "end": 94.14,
          "en": "when the form is submitted before console logging the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.14,
          "end": 98.793,
          "en": "we could check if data.password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.75,
          "end": 103.173,
          "en": "since I'm using password as a name here on this input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.75999999999999,
          "end": 108.15,
          "en": "is not equal to data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.15,
          "end": 112.413,
          "en": "And then here it's the confirm-password prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 113.31,
          "end": 116.22,
          "en": "And since it includes a dash, I must access it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.22,
          "end": 120.06,
          "en": "with this notation using these square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120.06,
          "end": 122.73,
          "en": "because the dot notation would not work here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 122.73,
          "end": 125.43299999999999,
          "en": "because this dash is an invalid character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 126.27,
          "end": 129.123,
          "en": "That's why I'm using the square bracket notation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.02,
          "end": 133.89,
          "en": "And I'm accessing the property confirmed-password here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.89,
          "end": 136.29,
          "en": "because that's the name I assigned here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.29,
          "end": 138.573,
          "en": "to this confirm password input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 141,
          "end": 141.84,
          "en": "So now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.84,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "I'm checking for the quality of these two entered values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 149.1,
          "en": "and if they're not equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.1,
          "end": 154.1,
          "en": "I can return to not execute any further code and make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.2,
          "end": 157.41,
          "en": "that this code doesn't get executed, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.41,
          "end": 160.2,
          "en": "And I can use this newly added state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.2,
          "end": 163.323,
          "en": "and set PasswordsAreNotEqual to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.84,
          "end": 169.95,
          "en": "So with that, I am blending my own validation logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 169.95,
          "end": 171.69299999999998,
          "en": "into this built-in logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 173.52,
          "end": 175.47,
          "en": "And now we can use PasswordsAreNotEqual",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 176.567,
          "end": 179.103,
          "en": "to show an error message if that's the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 180.06,
          "end": 182.04,
          "en": "For that, below this input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 182.04,
          "end": 185.46,
          "en": "this confirm-password input, I can add another div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 185.46,
          "end": 189.27,
          "en": "with that class name of control-error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.27,
          "end": 192.33,
          "en": "and then here check if passwords are not equal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.33,
          "end": 194.61,
          "en": "in which case I'll output an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 194.61,
          "end": 198.183,
          "en": "where I'll say passwords must match.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.87,
          "end": 205.65,
          "en": "With that, if I save this and I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 205.65,
          "end": 209.82,
          "en": "I still get the standard checks performed by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 209.82,
          "end": 212.55,
          "en": "But if I now fill out the form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 212.55,
          "end": 216.63,
          "en": "but I am having different passwords here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 216.63,
          "end": 219.27,
          "en": "and of course here I have a little error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 219.27,
          "end": 223.26,
          "en": "that should also be of type=password here in my code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 223.26,
          "end": 227.34,
          "en": "it should already be fixed in the code I provided to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 227.34,
          "end": 229.8,
          "en": "so that the input is hidden.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 229.8,
          "end": 232.9,
          "en": "But either way, if I enter a totally different value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 233.76,
          "end": 237.21,
          "en": "and I then fill out the rest of the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 237.21,
          "end": 239.94,
          "en": "you will, of course, see that now if I click sign up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 239.94,
          "end": 242.37,
          "en": "we still don't get the log here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 242.37,
          "end": 244.14,
          "en": "but instead we get this error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 244.14,
          "end": 246.33,
          "en": "because of the custom logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 246.33,
          "end": 249.063,
          "en": "which we now also added to this form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 250.08,
          "end": 252.48,
          "en": "And that is, of course, something you can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 252.48,
          "end": 254.52,
          "en": "and that's why I'm showing this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 254.52,
          "end": 258.36,
          "en": "You are not limited to the built-in validation features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 258.36,
          "end": 262.41,
          "en": "just because you're also using those, but you can instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 262.41,
          "end": 266.733,
          "en": "also add your own custom validation logic to this form.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}